cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MC-DRIVER in academic work, please cite it as below. If you improve the code, please report your changes back to the author (and, per the GPL-3.0 license, distribute derivative works under the same license)."
title: "MC-DRIVER: a site-list Monte-Carlo driver (GC + VC-SGC) for hydrogen on the Ni/NiH octahedral sublattice, coupled to LAMMPS"
abstract: >-
  MC-DRIVER computes the relationship between the hydrogen chemical potential
  and concentration on the octahedral interstitial sublattice of fcc Ni /
  rock-salt NiH. It implements grand-canonical (GC) and variance-constrained
  semi-grand-canonical (VC-SGC) Monte-Carlo sampling with energies supplied by
  LAMMPS, and is validated against analytic (Langmuir) and exact-enumeration
  benchmarks plus a Ni-H physical anchor.
type: software
